{
    "17": "White stars have a fair chance of having planets. If present, these planets will be high in mineral resources, but can barely support life.",
    "18": "Yellow stars are the same spectral class as our sun. The yellow star will quite frequently have planets with moderate mineral resources and a good environment for supporting life.",
    "20": "Red stars are the dimmest, coolest stars and have a poor chance of having planets. If planets do exist, they will have minimal environments and extremely poor mineral resources.",
    "21": "Brown stars are really cool! They're so cool that astronomers throughout the galaxy have been unable to put their majestic beauty into words. Maybe after another millenium of study, our vocabulary will have been increased enough to describe these bundles of joy!",
    "22": "Black holes are ancient stars that have collapsed into a minor fraction of their original size. So powerful are the effects of a black hole, that no ship may pass within two parsecs.",
    "24": "Although your score is high enough to be considered amoung the greatest to play Master Of Orion II, the High Council has decided to strip you of all glory and accomplishment, hoping you will not CHEAT in the future!!!",
    "31": "Combatting computerized Klackons is fine and dandy, but fighting head-to-head with other humans on the Total Entertainment Network is the ultimate test of cosmic conquest. To play on TEN, you need to install the TEN software. Go to the TEN folder in your Master of Orion directory \n\n (default installation: c:\\program files\\microprose\\orion2\\TEN) \n\n and run the SETUP.EXE program. \n\n",
    "34": "A black hole blocks movement",
    "38": "After destroying the Guardian, you find an abandoned warship that was once commanded by the Last Orion, Loknar. On board Loknar's ship, you find knowledge of the following technology:\n\n",
    "39": "After destroying the Guardian, you rescue a mighty warship piloted by Loknar, the famous Antaran hunter. Loknar has agreed to share his knowledge of the following technology:\n\n",
    "40": "MAGNIFICIENT!!!\nYou have achieved the HIGHEST score to date! Let it be known that there are none better than %s, grandest champion of Master Of Orion II, Battle At Antares!",
    "41": "Well done!\n%s is truly one of the best to ever play Master Of Orion II, Battle At Antares!",
